Product Requirements Document (PRD)
Module: Authentication for Secure Chat Webapp
1 — Overview

The Authentication Module ensures that only verified users can access the secure chat system. It provides login, registration, session management, and secure user identity verification. This module serves as the foundation for all other modules (contacts, messaging, file sharing, presence, etc.).

2 — Goals

Allow users to securely register and log in.

Maintain authenticated sessions with JWT or sessions.

Protect all subsequent APIs (contacts, messaging, file sharing) via middleware.

Enable easy integration with multi-device and socket-based real-time features.

Ensure data privacy and security in user credentials and session tokens.

3 — Functional Requirements
Feature	Description	Priority
User Registration	New users can create an account with username, email, and password. Passwords are hashed (bcrypt).	High
User Login	Existing users can log in with email/username + password.	High
Session Management	JWT issued on login, valid for a configurable period.	High
Token Refresh	Optional refresh token endpoint for long-lived sessions.	Medium
Password Recovery	Users can reset passwords via email verification.	Medium
Secure API Access	All protected endpoints require JWT auth middleware.	High
Rate Limiting	Prevent brute force login attempts.	Medium
Input Validation	Ensure usernames, emails, and passwords meet format rules.	High
4 — User Stories

Registration

As a new user, I want to create an account with a username, email, and password so I can log in later.

Workflow:

User sends POST /auth/signup with credentials.

Backend validates input, hashes password, stores user in DB.

Backend returns success with optional JWT.

Login

As a registered user, I want to log in securely so I can access the chat app.

Workflow:

User sends POST /auth/login with email/username and password.

Backend validates credentials.

If valid, backend issues JWT and returns user profile.

Session Validation

Every protected API (contacts, chat, files) checks for valid JWT via middleware.

JWT expiry handled; optional refresh token endpoint.

Password Reset

Users can request a password reset link via email (POST /auth/password-reset).

Link contains a time-limited token.

User submits new password via POST /auth/password-reset/confirm.

5 — Non-Functional Requirements

Security:

Passwords stored hashed (bcrypt/scrypt/argon2).

JWT signed with strong secret key.

HTTPS enforced.

Rate-limiting login attempts.

Scalability:

Support thousands of concurrent sessions.

Maintainability:

Controllers, routes, validators, and middlewares separated.

Performance:

Login/registration response under 500ms (excluding email delays).

6 — API Endpoints
Method	Endpoint	Description	Auth Required
POST	/auth/signup	Register new user	No
POST	/auth/login	Login user	No
POST	/auth/password-reset	Request reset link	No
POST	/auth/password-reset/confirm	Set new password	No
GET	/auth/profile	Get current user profile	Yes
POST	/auth/refresh-token	Refresh JWT	Optional

