7 — Database Design

User Model (user.models.js)

const mongoose = require("mongoose");
const bcrypt = require("bcrypt");

const userSchema = new mongoose.Schema({
  username: { type: String, required: true, unique: true },
  email: { type: String, required: true, unique: true },
  password: { type: String, required: true },
  profileImage: { type: String, default: null },
  status: { type: String, enum: ["online", "offline"], default: "offline" }
}, { timestamps: true });

// Hash password before saving
userSchema.pre("save", async function(next) {
  if (this.isModified("password")) {
    this.password = await bcrypt.hash(this.password, 10);
  }
  next();
});

// Password validation
userSchema.methods.isValidPassword = async function(password) {
  return bcrypt.compare(password, this.password);
};

module.exports = mongoose.model("User", userSchema);

8 — Middleware

auth.middleware.js

Extract JWT from Authorization header.

Verify signature and expiry.

Attach user object (req.user) to request.

Reject unauthorized requests with 401.

validator.middleware.js

Validate registration/login input using Joi schema.

9 — Integration Points

Contacts: Use req.user.id for contact ownership.

Messaging: Only allow sending messages if JWT valid.

File Sharing: File upload endpoints require auth.

Presence: Socket.IO connections verified via JWT token.

10 — User Experience

On signup/login success, JWT stored in client (localStorage/sessionStorage).

Auto-login if JWT exists and valid.

Clear error messages for invalid credentials or duplicate registration.

Password reset link expires in configurable time (e.g., 15 minutes).

11 — Security Considerations

Use HTTPS for all endpoints.

Store JWT secret securely in .env.

Rate-limit login attempts per IP.

Do not return password hashes in any API response.

Optional: 2FA support for future enhancement.

12 — Future Enhancements

2FA/MFA for login.

OAuth/social login integration (Google, Apple).

Device management (active sessions view, revoke).

Password strength meter on frontend.